< **Proof skeleton.** Conditional on A = s: U_r F = s·U_r H for the 2d+2 linear rows, v_r(b,k)/s = v_r(b/s,k/s), W^F = s^(2d) W^H, the type indicator and the selector are scale-invariant (D_(sf) = s·D_f since the admissible-λ set in ST (5) is a down-set). Mixing over A gives, for the selected, unselected and failure products alike, B^F_r(b,k) = E[A^(−2) B^H_r(b/A, k/A)], the two-height kernel K^F = E[A^(−2) K^H(·/A)], and ν_F(ℓ) = E[A^(−1) ν_H(ℓ/A)], m_F(t) = E[m_H(t/A)] (AMP (9)–(10) for general A, same proof). (1): at every fiber with k > 0 the A-integrands are bounded functions of A for every law, because SG's covariance floor and the pinned fourth row 12k give exp(−c k²/A²) as A → 0 and explicit negative powers as A → ∞; dominated convergence then transfers SG's pointwise limits. (2): substitute b = Ab′, k = Ak′ at fixed A (Jacobian A², no integrability of A at infinity used) and apply Tonelli; necessity uses (1) and c_q > 0. (3): the near part of G is bounded by (1/3)∫ k^(−2/3) H_SG from SG's near representation; the far part needs ν_(H,far)(u) ≤ C(1+u)^(2d) e^(−cu²) for all u > 0, which SG displays only on (0, 1] and which is re-derived by SG's own separated-pair argument keeping ℓ inside the Gaussian exponent (needed because small amplitudes probe large H-lifetimes); then A^(−2/3) G dominates and g(ℓ/A) → C_H pointwise. (4): Fatou with liminf ≥ E[A^(−2/3)] C_H = ∞.
